{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he harnessed his chariot.</b> He himself (Mekhilta)." "<b>And his people he took with him.</b> He drew them with words: 'Let us take our wealth and send them off. Come with me, and I will not conduct myself toward you as other kings do — the way of other kings is that their servants go before them in battle, but I will go first before you, as it says, ״וּפַרְעֹה הִקְרִיב״ — he brought forward himself and hurried ahead of his troops. The way of other kings is to take spoil first, as he chooses; I will share equally with you in the portion,' as it says, ״אֲחַלֵּק שָׁלָל״ (Exodus 15)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:04.200327740Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}